From 825aa49b87bcb88beabe27c87f14ecc15ece9865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sam <sam@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:07:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(cli): mid-stream resilience + live streaming display

Modeled on Gemini CLI's mid-stream retries (geminiChat.ts):

- processStreamingResponse consumes the stream through
  consumeStreamWithResilience (new streamResilience.ts): retryable
  mid-stream failures (429, 5xx, dropped connections) are retried up to
  3 times with 1s/2s/4s backoff instead of surfacing an error immediately
- continuation: when the failed attempt produced a partial answer, the
  retry sends it back as an assistant prefill so the model CONTINUES
  where it stopped (no regeneration, no duplicated content - the
  accumulated state now persists across attempts); a thinking-only or
  empty stream is retried with an explicit "provide your final answer"
  nudge instead of returning silence, and the error surfaces once the
  retry budget is exhausted
- per-chunk idle watchdog (default 120s, CONTINUE_CLI_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS,
  0 = off): a stalled/overloaded server is treated as a retryable
  failure instead of hanging the session forever
- onStreamReset callback lets the UI clear the partial display of a
  discarded attempt (Gemini's RETRY event pattern)
- live streaming: the TUI now renders the in-progress assistant content,
  flushed at most every 120ms (bounded re-render cost) instead of only
  showing the reply when it completes
